WEBVTT

00:03:58.718 --> 00:04:00.429
in three in a half hours,

00:04:00.429 --> 00:04:02.566
that guy was drinking rat poison and brandy

00:04:02.566 --> 00:04:04.598
while he ran along the course.

00:04:04.598 --> 00:04:07.221
That was his idea of a performance-enhancing drug.

00:04:07.221 --> 00:04:09.284
(Laughter)

00:04:09.284 --> 00:04:10.972
Clearly, athletes have gotten more savvy

00:04:10.972 --> 00:04:13.446
about performance-enhancing drugs as well,

00:04:13.446 --> 00:04:15.717
and that's made a difference
in some sports at some times,

00:04:15.717 --> 00:04:18.004
but technology has made a difference in all sports,

00:04:18.004 --> 00:04:20.553
from faster skis to lighter shoes.

00:04:20.553 --> 00:04:23.693
Take a look at the record for
the 100-meter freestyle swim.

00:04:23.693 --> 00:04:26.340
The record is always trending downward,

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:29.090
but it's punctuated by these steep cliffs.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:32.011
This first cliff, in 1956, is the introduction